Setup Joystick lists the pad bindings.

In SDL GameController mode - the default, and this port's - SuperTux fixes the pad's
bindings in `src/control/game_controller_manager.cpp`, and Options, Setup Joystick
shows only the "Manual Configuration" toggle: nothing on any screen says which button
runs or looks around. Under `OOPS_TARGET` the screen lists them, read-only, in this
pad's button names.

--- a/src/supertux/menu/joystick_menu.cpp
+++ b/src/supertux/menu/joystick_menu.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,15 @@
   if (m_input_manager.use_game_controller())
   {
     m_joysticks_available = false;
+#ifdef OOPS_TARGET
+    // The console pad's bindings, read-only: `game_controller_manager.cpp` fixes them in
+    // this mode, and this screen otherwise showed nothing but the toggle above.
+    add_hl();
+    add_inactive(_("Left stick / D-pad: walk, duck, climb, enter doors"));
+    add_inactive(_("Cross: jump    Square: run, grab, fire"));
+    add_inactive(_("Right stick, L1 / R1: look around"));
+    add_inactive(_("Options: pause    Circle: back in menus"));
+#endif
   }
   else
   {
